{
 "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
 "version": 1,
 "notes": "Boot a Jack*Bot ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled (the driver declares none); the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, wait out the power-up mechanism homing (no power-up report follows on this ROM, so two Enters reach the main menu) and open the service menu. Start T.4 SOLENOID TEST in repeat mode and step it with Up 40 times so it wraps. In repeat mode the ROM pulses the selected driver and prints its name and wire colours, so each step pairs a printed name with the public address PinMAME published. The checkpoint fails the run unless T.4 pulses a solenoid.",
 "initial_switches": [
  {
   "switch": 22,
   "state": 0
  }
 ],
